# Environment Variable Rules

## Core Principle

If an environment variable is missing or incorrect, the application must fail at **build time**, not at runtime.
For this reason, all env vars are validated with Zod through `src/env.ts`.

## src/env.ts Structure (@t3-oss/env-nextjs)

```ts
// src/env.ts
import { createEnv } from "@t3-oss/env-nextjs"
import { z } from "zod"

export const env = createEnv({
  server: {
    DATABASE_URL: z.string().url(),
    REDIS_URL: z.string().url(),
    AUTH_SECRET: z.string().min(32),
    MINIO_ENDPOINT: z.string(),
    MINIO_ACCESS_KEY: z.string(),
    MINIO_SECRET_KEY: z.string(),
    MINIO_BUCKET: z.string(),
  },
  client: {
    NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL: z.string().url(),
  },
  runtimeEnv: {
    DATABASE_URL: process.env.DATABASE_URL,
    REDIS_URL: process.env.REDIS_URL,
    AUTH_SECRET: process.env.AUTH_SECRET,
    MINIO_ENDPOINT: process.env.MINIO_ENDPOINT,
    MINIO_ACCESS_KEY: process.env.MINIO_ACCESS_KEY,
    MINIO_SECRET_KEY: process.env.MINIO_SECRET_KEY,
    MINIO_BUCKET: process.env.MINIO_BUCKET,
    NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL,
  },
})
```

## Usage Rules

```ts
// Correct — always access through env.ts
import { env } from "@/env"
const db = new PrismaClient({ datasourceUrl: env.DATABASE_URL })

// Wrong — do not use process.env directly
const db = new PrismaClient({ datasourceUrl: process.env.DATABASE_URL })
```

## .env Files

| File | Purpose | Committed to repo? |
|------|---------|-------------------|
| `.env.example` | Shows which variables are required; no actual values | ✅ Yes |
| `.env` | Local development values | ❌ No |
| `.env.test` | Test environment values | ❌ No |

`.env.example` must always be kept up to date — add any new env var here when you add it.

## Management in Coolify

- All production values are set via Coolify UI
- The deploy pipeline runs `src/env.ts` validation during build
- If a value is missing, the build fails — bad config never reaches production

## Security

- Variables without the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix do not enter the client bundle
- Never make secrets (AUTH_SECRET, MINIO_SECRET_KEY, etc.) `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
- Add `.env` to `.gitignore` (Next.js adds it by default)
